45, 670]], [[527, 691], [490, 677], [456, 665], [420, 655], [390, 647], [330, 648], [380, 681], [444, 703], [480, 714], [517, 721]], [[519, 790], [423, 772], [327, 756], [260, 752], [210, 755], [265, 770], [321, 788], [417, 808], [513, 822]]], "star_names": [{"star": 71683, "name": "Mirka", "gloss": "the Bride's Heart"}, {"star": 71908, "name": "Tessu", "gloss": "the Holdfast"}], "myth": "Ulsena was a kelp-woman who lived in the cold shallows under the cliffs. One hot, calm day, which the old ones say never comes here, she climbed onto the rocks and married Ristan, a fisherman of the north skerry. He went out the next spring and the gale Tavo came laughing across the water and took his boat. Ulsena waited in the shallows. When no boat came back she did what kelp does when it wants the light. She grew. Her stalk went up past the seals, past the gulls, and when it left the water it kept going, because Aun had cut the string and nothing held the sky down any more. Her bulb is the crown at the top. Her long brown fronds still sway in the Unflown. Mother Hesk counts her turns and says she has not yet found him. Sailors say that on a calm night, if you hear a slow creak over the water, it is Ulsena, still looking.", "verse": "Her stalk climbs past gulls,\nthrough the cut string's empty air,\nshe sways, still searching.", "gods": ["Aun", "Hesk", "Tavo"]}, "cost": 0.006958969999999999, "secs": 52.7, "history": ["redrawn round 1"]}